From: Arjan van de Ven <arjan@linux.intel.com>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pci: Set PME_TIMEOUT to 4000ms to reduce spurious wakeups

Clear Linux optimization: poll PME events every 4 seconds instead of 1.
Reduces unnecessary system wakeups on boards where PCIe PME polling can
trigger spuriously and prevent deep CPU C-states.

Sourced from linux-tkg clear-patches (Arjan van de Ven / Clear Linux).

Forward-Port-Notes: drivers/pci/pci.c
---
 drivers/pci/pci.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pci.c b/drivers/pci/pci.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci.c
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ struct pci_pme_device {
 	struct pci_dev *dev;
 };

-#define PME_TIMEOUT 1000 /* How long between PME checks */
+#define PME_TIMEOUT 4000 /* How long between PME checks */

 /*
  * Following exit from Conventional Reset, devices must be ready within 1 sec
